# This repository (the slack-knowledge-sync definition) is checked out at the agent's
# HOME root (/home/agent), which also contains secrets and runtime state (.ssh, .claude,
# .config, work/, ...). To make `git add -A` safe and never capture those, ignore
# EVERYTHING at the top level by default, then re-include only the definition files this
# repo actually tracks.
#
# NOTE: NOTHING under work/ is tracked — it is all runtime state, seeded on a fresh
# volume from the templates in ONBOARDING.md. That matters more here than for most
# agents: work/ holds what this agent captured from one person's Slack, including the
# knowledge base itself (work/knowledge/). Captured content must never reach this public
# definition repo, so neither work/ nor any knowledge/ directory is ever re-included.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/README.md
!/ONBOARDING.md
!/kit.yaml
!/VERSION
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/LICENSE
!/docs/
!/scripts/
!/.github/

# Never track these even if a future allowlist entry would pull them in.
/work/
/knowledge/
knowledge/
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
